Subject: Register molecules with the avogadrolibs 2 layer manager so the viewer draws them

avogadrolibs 2 keeps whether a scene plugin is enabled per molecule in
its layer manager, and only a molecule handed to RWLayerManager::addMolecule
becomes the active one. KalziumGLWidget never did that, so every
setEnabled() was a no-op, activeScenePlugins() stayed empty and the
Molecular Editor drew nothing. The widget now registers each molecule it
is given, enables the style the dialog chose by the plugin's name() and
reapplies it on every new molecule. The view also takes an opaque
background from the palette's Base colour, since the scene default is
transparent and shows the window behind it on Wayland.

